allId":"call_p0FI56OPSQkNJkNpiifNhJFu|fc_0724ab837424664b016a958d406fd887d29dab75fe77548cb9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/schema_migration/migration_notes.md#3D98]\n1:# Order API Migration Notes\n2:\n3:Supported inputs:\n4:- Legacy v1 payloads use `id`, `customer_id`, `customer_name`, `items`, `ship_to`, and optional `shipping_method`.\n5:- Legacy v1.1 payloads may use `shipping` instead of `shipping_method`, and `ship_to.postalCode` instead of `ship_to.postal`.\n6:- Legacy v1.2 payloads may use `order_ref`, `customer.id`, `customer.name`, `lines`, and `shipTo`. Line items may use `unit_price_cents` instead of `price_cents`.\n7:- Public v2 payloads already have `orderId`, `buyer`, `lineItems`, `shipping`, and `metadata`; conversion must be idempotent.\n8:\n9:Field mapping:\n10:- `id` -> `orderId`\n11:- `order_ref` -> `orderId`\n12:- `customer_id` -> `buyer.id`\n13:- `customer_name` -> `buyer.displayName`\n14:- `customer.id` -> `buyer.id`\n15:- `customer.name` -> `buyer.displayName`\n16:- `lines` -> `lineItems`\n17:- each item `qty` -> `quantity` as an integer\n18:- each item `price_cents` -> `unitPriceCents` as an integer\n19:- each item `unit_price_cents` -> `unitPriceCents` as an integer\n20:- `ship_to.postal` or `ship_to.postalCode` -> `shipping.address.postalCode`\n21:- `shipTo.postal_code` -> `shipping.address.postalCode`\n22:- blank or null shipping method -> `standard`\n23:\n24:Unknown legacy fields should be preserved in `metadata.unknownFields` unless the PII policy excludes them.\n25:\n26:Errors from `convert_many` should include `index`, `path`, and `error`, and conversion should continue after bad records.\n27:\n28:Warnings:\n29:- `convert_many` should return `(converted, errors, warnings)` when warnings are present, or preserve backward compatibility by allowing callers to unpack the first two values.\n30:- A warning should include `index`, `path`, and `warning`.\n31:- Dropped PII and preserved unknown fields should be counted